The difference between female and male GPAs is only 0.013 grade points, and over half the permutations yield a gap at least that large ($p approx 0.53$). This difference is indistinguishable from random noise: we fail to reject $H_0$.

This #strong[permutation test] contains the entire logic of statistical inference. Formal statistical tests differ only in using mathematical distributions ($t$, $F$, $chi^2$) to derive the null distribution analytically.

=== The p-value
<the-p-value>
The #strong[$p$-value] is the probability of obtaining test results at least as extreme as the results actually observed, #emph[under the assumption that the null hypothesis is true].

- When $p < alpha$ (conventionally $alpha = 0.05$), the result is declared #strong[statistically significant], and we reject $H_0$.
- When $p gt.eq alpha$, the data is deemed consistent with $H_0$. We do #emph[not] prove $H_0$ is true; we merely conclude that the evidence is insufficient to reject it.

