<fig-interaction>


Part-time students have lower wellbeing in both programmes, and the lines are close to parallel. In the formula, #NormalTok("C(programme) * C(study_mode)"); asks for both main effects and their interaction:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("model_2way ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" smf.ols(");#StringTok("\"wellbeing ~ C(programme) * C(study_mode)\"");#NormalTok(", data");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok("study).fit()");],
[#NormalTok("aov_2way ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" sm.stats.anova_lm(model_2way, typ");#OperatorTok("=");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(")");],
[#BuiltInTok("print");#NormalTok("(aov_2way)");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("                                  sum_sq     df          F    PR(>F)");],
[#NormalTok("C(programme)                  156.553032    1.0   1.105982  0.293383");],
[#NormalTok("C(study_mode)                1640.156694    1.0  11.587025  0.000709");],
[#NormalTok("C(programme):C(study_mode)    118.619402    1.0   0.837997  0.360341");],
[#NormalTok("Residual                    84364.487300  596.0        NaN       NaN");],));
