The first hours of study make a real difference; the curve then flattens, and reaches its highest point at about 32 hours a week, beyond which more study brings nothing extra. Economists call this #strong[diminishing returns], and it is worth knowing for any student tempted to study all night instead of sleeping.

=== Interactions
<interactions>
The effect of supervisor support need not be the same for every student. An #strong[interaction] term lets the effect of one predictor depend on another. In the formula, #NormalTok("support_c * C(programme)"); gives the effect of support, the effect of programme, and how the effect of support differs between programmes. To make the coefficients easier to read, support is first #strong[centred]: the average is subtracted, so that zero means "average support":

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("study[");#StringTok("\"support_c\"");#NormalTok("] ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" study[");#StringTok("\"support\"");#NormalTok("] ");#OperatorTok("-");#NormalTok(" study[");#StringTok("\"support\"");#NormalTok("].mean()");],
[#NormalTok("gpa_interaction ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" smf.ols(");#StringTok("\"gpa ~ support_c * C(programme) + sleep_hours + study_hours\"");#NormalTok(", data");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok("study).fit()");],
[#BuiltInTok("print");#NormalTok("(gpa_interaction.summary().tables[");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("])");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("=================================================================================================");],
[#NormalTok("                                    coef    std err          t      P>|t|      [0.025      0.975]");],
[#NormalTok("-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------");],
[#NormalTok("Intercept                         2.1546      0.112     19.207      0.000       1.934       2.375");],
[#NormalTok("C(programme)[T.PhD]               0.0117      0.026      0.449      0.654      -0.040       0.063");],
[#NormalTok("support_c                         0.1021      0.018      5.552      0.000       0.066       0.138");],
[#NormalTok("support_c:C(programme)[T.PhD]     0.1342      0.036      3.743      0.000       0.064       0.205");],
[#NormalTok("sleep_hours                       0.1177      0.014      8.385      0.000       0.090       0.145");],
[#NormalTok("study_hours                       0.0066      0.001      5.914      0.000       0.004       0.009");],
[#NormalTok("=================================================================================================");],));
]
]
For Master's students (the reference category), each point of support goes with a GPA about 0.10 higher. The interaction coefficient says that for PhD students the effect is larger, making it about 0.24. Supervisor support matters about 2.3 times as much for PhD students, which makes sense: a PhD depends more heavily on the supervisor.

=== Model diagnostics
<model-diagnostics>
Linear regression assumes that the relationship is linear (or modelled as curved, as above), that the residuals have similar spread everywhere (homoscedasticity), and that they are roughly normal. Violations show up as patterns in a plot of the residuals against the fitted values. It helps to know what those patterns look like before judging a real model, and simulated data can show them:

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("np.random.seed(");#DecValTok("10");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("x_sim ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" np.random.uniform(");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("10");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("200");#NormalTok(")");],
[],
[#NormalTok("sim_cases ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" {");],
[#NormalTok("    ");#StringTok("\"Assumptions met\"");#NormalTok(": ");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" ");#FloatTok("0.5");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("*");#NormalTok(" x_sim ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" np.random.normal(");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("200");#NormalTok("),");],
[#NormalTok("    ");#StringTok("\"Curved\"");#NormalTok(": ");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" ");#FloatTok("0.25");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("*");#NormalTok(" (x_sim");#OperatorTok("**");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(") ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" np.random.normal(");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("200");#NormalTok("),");],
[#NormalTok("    ");#StringTok("\"Spread increases\"");#NormalTok(": ");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" ");#FloatTok("0.5");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("*");#NormalTok(" x_sim ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" np.random.normal(");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("0.2");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("+");#NormalTok(" ");#FloatTok("0.3");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("*");#NormalTok(" x_sim, ");#DecValTok("200");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("}");],
[],
[#NormalTok("fig, axes ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" plt.subplots(");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("3");#NormalTok(", figsize");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok("(");#DecValTok("8");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("3");#NormalTok("), sharey");#OperatorTok("=");#VariableTok("True");#NormalTok(")");],
