Clustering works with #strong[distances] between students: how different two students' profiles are. Caffeine is measured in hundreds of milligrams and sleep in single hours, so without adjustment caffeine would dominate every distance. #NormalTok("StandardScaler"); turns every variable into z-scores (Chapter 6), so each counts equally.

=== k-means clustering
<k-means-clustering>
#strong[k-means] is the most widely used clustering method. The researcher chooses the number of clusters, $k$, and the algorithm places $k$ starting points at random, assigns each student to the nearest point, moves each point to the centre (the mean) of its students, and repeats the last two steps until nothing changes. In #NormalTok("scikit-learn");, #NormalTok("n_init=25"); runs the algorithm from 25 different starting seeds and keeps the best partition.

=== The number of clusters
<the-number-of-clusters>
As with components, no single rule decides the number of clusters, and two guides are common. The #strong[elbow method] uses the fact that the total distance of students from their cluster centres (inertia) falls as $k$ grows, and looks for the point where adding clusters stops helping much. The #strong[silhouette] measures, for each student, how much closer they are to their own cluster than to the next nearest one, from −1 to 1; a higher average silhouette means clearer clusters.

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("inertias ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" []");],
[#NormalTok("silhouettes ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" []");],
[#NormalTok("k_range ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" ");#BuiltInTok("range");#NormalTok("(");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("9");#NormalTok(")");],
[],
[#ControlFlowTok("for");#NormalTok(" k ");#KeywordTok("in");#NormalTok(" k_range:");],
[#NormalTok("    km ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" KMeans(n_clusters");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok("k, n_init");#OperatorTok("=");#DecValTok("25");#NormalTok(", random_state");#OperatorTok("=");#DecValTok("123");#NormalTok(").fit(profile_scaled)");],
[#NormalTok("    inertias.append(km.inertia_)");],
[#NormalTok("    silhouettes.append(silhouette_score(profile_scaled, km.labels_))");],
[],
[#NormalTok("fig, axes ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" plt.subplots(");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(", figsize");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok("(");#DecValTok("8");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.4");#NormalTok("))");],
