]
]
Two details matter. The outcome is coded as binary ($1$ for "Yes", $0$ for "No"), making "Yes" (considering dropout) the positive event to detect. And the workshop variables are removed: the workshop took place after the first semester, so it would not be known when the prediction is made. Using information that would not be available at the time of prediction is a form of #strong[data leakage], and it makes a model look better than it can ever be in practice.

