== Exercises
<exercises-10>
The #link("../playground/chapter11.html")[playground] has these and more, with hints and solutions.

+ Remove the questionnaire scores (#NormalTok("stress");, #NormalTok("burnout");, #NormalTok("support");, #NormalTok("satisfaction");) from #NormalTok("dropout_data"); and fit the logistic regression pipeline again. Report how much the cross-validated AUC falls, and what that says about the questionnaire.
+ Split the data 80/20 instead of 75/25 with a different random state (e.g.~#NormalTok("random_state=7");), and describe how much the test AUC of the logistic model changes, and why it might.
