== Imbalanced outcomes
<imbalanced-outcomes>
When one outcome is rare, as considering dropout is, models tend to predict the common one. Besides moving the threshold, there are two other common remedies. #strong[Resampling] changes the training data so that the classes are balanced: #strong[upsampling] repeats rare-class students, #strong[downsampling] drops common-class students, and #strong[SMOTE] creates new, artificial rare-class students between existing ones. #strong[Class weights] instead make mistakes on the rare class count more when the model is fitted, and scikit-learn models support them directly via #NormalTok("class_weight='balanced'");:

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("balanced_pipe ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" Pipeline([");],
