The two tight groups become clusters 0 and 1, and the two isolated points are labelled -1: noise. k-means with two clusters would have had to put the isolated points into one of the groups.

=== Choosing eps
<choosing-eps>
The result depends heavily on #NormalTok("eps");. A common guide is the #strong[k-nearest-neighbour distance plot]: for each case, the distance to its $k$-th nearest neighbour, sorted from smallest to largest. Most cases have close neighbours; the curve bends sharply upwards where the isolated cases begin, and that bend suggests a value for #NormalTok("eps");. With #NormalTok("min_samples"); set to 8, a common choice for data with seven variables (about the number of variables plus one or more), the plot uses $k = 7$:

#Skylighting(([#ImportTok("from");#NormalTok(" sklearn.neighbors ");#ImportTok("import");#NormalTok(" NearestNeighbors");],
[],
[#NormalTok("nbrs ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors");#OperatorTok("=");#DecValTok("7");#NormalTok(").fit(profile_data)");],
[#NormalTok("distances, _ ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" nbrs.kneighbors(profile_data)");],
[#NormalTok("k_distances ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" np.sort(distances[:, ");#OperatorTok("-");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("])");],
[],
[#NormalTok("fig, ax ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" plt.subplots(figsize");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok("(");#DecValTok("6");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.5");#NormalTok("))");],
[#NormalTok("ax.plot(k_distances, color");#OperatorTok("=");#StringTok("'#2f6793'");#NormalTok(", linewidth");#OperatorTok("=");#FloatTok("1.5");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("ax.axhline(");#FloatTok("2.0");#NormalTok(", color");#OperatorTok("=");#StringTok("'grey'");#NormalTok(", linestyle");#OperatorTok("=");#StringTok("'--'");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("ax.set_xlabel(");#StringTok("'Students (sorted by distance)'");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("ax.set_ylabel(");#StringTok("'7-NN distance'");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("plt.show()");],));
#figure([
#box(image("14-advanced-clustering_files/figure-typst/fig-knndist-output-1.svg", alt: "A curve that rises slowly over most of the students, then bends sharply upwards for the last few. A horizontal dashed line at 2 crosses the curve where it starts to bend."))
], caption: figure.caption(
