== Decomposition
<decomposition>
#strong[Decomposition] recovers the parts of a pattern from an observed series: a smooth #strong[trend], a repeating #strong[seasonal] component, and the #strong[remainder], what is left over, which corresponds to the noise of #ref(<fig-parts>, supplement: [Figure]). #strong[STL] (seasonal and trend decomposition using loess) is a flexible, widely used method available in #NormalTok("statsmodels.tsa.seasonal.STL");. Setting #NormalTok("period=52"); specifies the annual cycle, and #NormalTok("robust=True"); prevents extreme weeks from distorting the trend:

