The STL and ETS model is best: its forecasts are off by 6.8 visits a week on average (MAE), against 7.0 for the seasonal naive benchmark, which simply repeats the previous year. The mean and naive methods, which ignore the seasonal pattern, are far worse. The Fourier model does worse than the seasonal naive benchmark: the counselling service's pattern has sharp steps (the summer drop happens from one week to the next), and smooth waves struggle to follow them. #ref(<fig-test-forecasts>, supplement: [Figure]) compares the two best models with the actual visits.

