=== References and citations
<references-and-citations>
The bibliography file uses the standard #strong[BibTeX] format, which almost every reference manager (Zotero, Mendeley, EndNote) can export, and Google Scholar can provide for any paper:

#Skylighting(([#VariableTok("@book");#NormalTok("{");#OtherTok("wickham2023");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#DataTypeTok("author");#NormalTok("    = {Wickham, Hadley and Çetinkaya-Rundel, Mine and Grolemund, Garrett},");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#DataTypeTok("title");#NormalTok("     = {R for Data Science},");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#DataTypeTok("publisher");#NormalTok(" = {O'Reilly Media},");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#DataTypeTok("year");#NormalTok("      = {2023}");],
[#NormalTok("}");],));
The citation key, #NormalTok("wickham2023");, follows the #NormalTok("@"); symbol in the text. A #NormalTok("csl:"); line in the YAML header chooses the citation style (APA 7th, Vancouver, Harvard, IEEE, or journal-specific styles), meaning that changing target journals never requires reformatting references by hand.

=== Equations
<equations>
Equations are written in standard #strong[LaTeX] notation between dollar signs: #NormalTok("$\\bar{x} = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum x_i$"); inside a sentence gives $macron(x) = 1 / n sum x_i$, and double dollar signs set an equation on its own line:

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("$$");],
[#NormalTok("\\text{logit}(p) = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 \\times \\text{stress} + \\beta_2 \\times \\text{support}");],
[#NormalTok("$$");],));
$ upright("logit") \( p \) = beta_0 + beta_1 times upright("stress") + beta_2 times upright("support") $

The same LaTeX notation renders identically across HTML, Word, and PDF output.

=== Output formats
<output-formats>
Changing one line in the YAML header switches the entire document's target:

#figure([
#table(
  columns: (33.33%, 33.33%, 33.33%),
  align: (auto,auto,auto,),
  table.header([Format], [YAML], [Notes],),
  table.hline(),
  [Web page], [#NormalTok("format: html");], [Interactive; ideal for supplementary websites and sharing findings],
  [Word], [#NormalTok("format: docx");], [For supervisory review; #NormalTok("reference-doc: template.docx"); applies university formatting],
  [PDF], [#NormalTok("format: pdf"); or #NormalTok("format: typst");], [Typeset PDF; Typst is lightning-fast and modern],
  [Slides], [#NormalTok("format: revealjs");], [For conference presentations and thesis defenses],
)
], caption: figure.caption(
position: top, 
[
Common Quarto output formats
]), 
kind: "quarto-float-tbl", 
supplement: "Table", 
)
<tbl-formats>


Multiple formats can be specified at once, allowing a single #NormalTok("quarto render"); call to generate both an accessible HTML web page and a formal Word thesis draft.

