The code runs without error and the numbers look believable. However, the percentages sum to only 15.7%---the percentage of #emph[all] students who considered dropping out! Dividing by #NormalTok("len(students)"); divides by the global sample size rather than the faculty subgroup size.

The correct formulation computes the proportion #emph[within] each faculty:

#Skylighting(([#CommentTok("# Correct calculation:");],
[#NormalTok("correct ");#OperatorTok("=");#NormalTok(" (");],
[#NormalTok("    students.groupby(");#StringTok("'faculty'");#NormalTok(")[");#StringTok("'considering_dropout'");#NormalTok("]");],
[#NormalTok("    .");#BuiltInTok("apply");#NormalTok("(");#KeywordTok("lambda");#NormalTok(" s: ");#DecValTok("100");#NormalTok(" ");#OperatorTok("*");#NormalTok(" (s ");#OperatorTok("==");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("'Yes'");#NormalTok(").mean())");],
[#NormalTok("    .reset_index(name");#OperatorTok("=");#StringTok("'percent'");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("    .");#BuiltInTok("round");#NormalTok("(");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("correct");],));
#table(
  columns: 3,
  align: (auto,auto,auto,),
  table.header(table.cell(align: right)[], table.cell(align: right)[faculty], table.cell(align: right)[percent],),
  table.hline(),
  table.cell(align: horizon)[0], [Education], [10.8],
  table.cell(align: horizon)[1], [Health Sciences], [18.8],
  table.cell(align: horizon)[2], [Humanities], [13.7],
  table.cell(align: horizon)[3], [Natural Sciences], [12.6],
  table.cell(align: horizon)[4], [Social Sciences], [18.1],
)
Because #NormalTok("(s == 'Yes')"); is a boolean series, its mean is the exact within-faculty proportion (Chapter 6). The assistant's error was not an obvious crash; it was a subtle conceptual mismatch.

Catching such errors requires four standard habits:

+ #strong[Test on toy data]: run code on a tiny 3-row DataFrame where you know the manual calculation.
+ #strong[Cross-check by alternative routes]: cross-tabulate counts with #NormalTok("pd.crosstab(students['faculty'], students['considering_dropout'], normalize='index')");.
+ #strong[Inspect library documentation]: verify parameters and return signatures in official docstrings.
+ #strong[Ask the assistant to explain]: requesting #emph["explain how the denominator is computed"] often exposes faulty logic immediately.

