= Appendix C: Python Packages
<sec-app-packages>
This appendix lists every Python scientific library used across the book: what it is for, the chapters that apply it, and the package version used when compiling this edition. Appendix A shows how to install all of them into a project virtual environment using #NormalTok("pip");.

In Python, a library (or package) is a reusable collection of modules, functions, classes, and documentation shared via the Python Package Index (PyPI). Python includes a robust standard library (#NormalTok("sys");, #NormalTok("os");, #NormalTok("math");, #NormalTok("json");, #NormalTok("datetime");) available without installation; third-party scientific packages are installed once via #NormalTok("pip install <package>"); and imported into your analysis sessions using #NormalTok("import <package>");.

