[#ControlFlowTok("return");#NormalTok(" weight_kg ");#OperatorTok("/");#NormalTok(" (height_m ");#OperatorTok("**");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok(")");],));
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("IndentationError: expected an indented block after function definition");],));
#strong[What it means:] Unlike R or C++ which use curly braces #NormalTok("{}"); to group code blocks, Python relies strictly on indentation (usually 4 spaces).

#strong[How to fix it:] - Indent all statements inside functions, loops, and conditional blocks by 4 spaces: #NormalTok("python   def calculate_bmi(weight_kg, height_m):       return weight_kg / (height_m**2)"); - Never mix tabs and spaces in the same file. In VS Code, ensure your indentation setting is set to "Spaces: 4".

